# Milestone: M3
# Covers: two Realms have isolated bindings; var defined in one realm is not
#         visible in another.
#
# blocked: T39 chk-runner host-driver/tunables extension not implemented
# matrix-row: chunk-lifecycle-realm
#
# Reason: chk runner currently drives a single REPL session via the standalone
# urbi binary. There is no host-driver hook to instantiate two Realms with
# isolated bindings and verify that bindings don't leak across them.
# Realm semantics are already verified by tests/unit/test_realm.c (landed at T14).
# T39 will add a tunables-header syntax to the chk runner allowing custom C
# host setup; T20 will provide the Strand C API.
#
# When T39 lands, implement this fixture by adding a host-driver section that
# creates two Realms, binds x=1 in the first, x=2 in the second, and verifies
# they remain isolated.
#
# Pseudo-host-driver (activate at T39):
#   URealm *r1 = urbi_realm_new(vm);
#   URealm *r2 = urbi_realm_new(vm);
#   urbi_realm_set_binding(r1, "x", val_1);
#   urbi_realm_set_binding(r2, "x", val_2);
#   --- Urbiscript source (run against r1 and r2 separately) ---
#   x
#   --- expected output (r1) ---
#   [00000001] 1
#   --- expected output (r2) ---
#   [00000001] 2
